      priceMovement: "Both BTC and ETH prices are highly sensitive to macroeconomic trends, regulatory news (like the CLARITY Act), institutional adoption, and market sentiment. They often show correlated price movements but can diverge based on specific ecosystem developments.",
      onChainMetrics: "Bitcoin\'s on-chain metrics include active addresses, transaction count, hash rate, and exchange flows. Ethereum\'s metrics include gas usage, unique active addresses, total value locked (TVL) in DeFi, and staking participation, all indicating robust network activity.",
      whaleActivity: "Both Bitcoin and Ethereum see significant \'whale\' (large holder) activity, with movements in large wallets often signaling potential market shifts or institutional accumulation/distribution.",
