    investorTakeaways: ["**Prioritize Robust Security Practices**: Implement multi-factor authentication, use strong unique passwords, and exercise extreme caution with links or unsolicited communications. For hardware wallets, buy directly from the manufacturer and verify authenticity.", "**Understand Self-Custody Risks**: While beneficial for control, self-custody carries the responsibility of being your own bank. Be aware of all potential attack vectors, including social engineering and supply chain compromises.", "**Stay Informed on On-Chain Forensics**: Familiarize yourself with the capabilities of blockchain analytics. While not a direct recovery tool for individual investors, understanding how funds are traced provides valuable context on market integrity.", "**Diversify Security Strategies**: Do not rely on a single security measure. Consider a combination of hardware wallets, cold storage, and trusted custodial solutions for different portions of your portfolio.", "**Monitor Regulatory Developments**: Increased scrutiny on crypto crime can lead to new regulations impacting exchanges and potentially the broader market. Stay updated on compliance changes."],
